Docker is a platform used to build, run, and manage containers.
Containers package an application with its dependencies.
Docker provides consistent environments across development and production.
Docker Image is a blueprint used to create containers.
Docker Container is a running instance of an image.
Dockerfile contains instructions to build an image.
Docker Hub is a registry for storing and sharing images.
Docker containers are lightweight and fast compared with virtual machines.
Common commands: docker build, docker run, docker ps, docker stop.
Docker is widely used in DevOps, CI/CD, microservices, and cloud deployments.